Z||000000||zeusrekning||05-30-2000||09:40 PM||||I went to the parts store today and when i got out i heard SHHHHHHHHHHH. I opened the hood and the hose going intothe intake manifold right above the ecm/distributer (whatever it is). Is it supposed to snap to gether and apart I don't know what happened?parts that fell out when i took it apart. O-ring and plastic cap with 3/8 " hole in it. there is a divider in the hole (-) ||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||05-31-2000||10:48 AM||||This must be the 2.5 engine, mine did the same thing. I believe that little coolant hose warms the manifold for better emission control. The V8 engines (and I assume the V6's too) have an exhaust crossover built into the manifold for the same purpose. To fix my leak, I found a hose nipple adapter with the right size pipe threads for the manifold and then clamped the hose onto this nipple with a worm screw type of hose clamp. It worked fine.||||reg||1
